<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ValidationRule xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description>, AND IT MUST STAY THAT WAY.
        ValidationRule.Description is capped at 255 characters. The full rationale below is
        operationally important, so it was moved here rather than trimmed; a comment is
        repo-only and is never sent to the Metadata API, so it can be as long as it needs to
        be. Do not paste this back into <description>.

        Decision D3 = declarative (Option 1): blocks Lead conversion unless Property Address
        and Email are both filled. Enforced at conversion ONLY IF the org setting
        shouldLeadConvertRequireValidation ("Require Validation for Converted Leads",
        Setup -> Lead Settings) is ON.

        NOT YET VERIFIED IN THE TARGET ORG as of this metadata-only build, the repo's
        settings/LeadConfig.settings-meta.xml snapshot shows it as true, but that file is
        forceignored (never deploys, may be a stale/different-org snapshot). If this setting
        is OFF, this rule fails OPEN silently (no gate) rather than failing closed. MUST
        verify in Setup before/at deploy per the design doc's pre-deploy checklist; remedy if
        off is a one-click setting change (safe today, Lead had zero validation rules before
        this change).

        This covers the standard Convert button and the API, not just the custom quick
        action, the declarative mechanism was chosen over an Apex pre-check for exactly that
        reason. Validation rules evaluate before after-update triggers, so if this rule
        fires, Database.convertLead is refused and LeadConvertTrigger/LeadConvertService
        never run, there is no partial-conversion state, only a refused conversion.

        errorDisplayField is Status (IsConverted has no direct UI surface to attach an error
        to on the standard Convert screen).
    -->
    <fullName>Property_And_Email_Required_To_Convert</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>Blocks Lead conversion unless Property Address and Email are both filled, subject to an org setting verified before deploy. See the XML comment in this file.</description>
    <errorConditionFormula>AND(
    RecordType.DeveloperName = &apos;Acquisition_Broker&apos;,
    ISCHANGED(IsConverted),
    IsConverted,
    OR(
        ISBLANK(Property_Address__c),
        ISBLANK(Email)
    )
)</errorConditionFormula>
    <errorDisplayField>Status</errorDisplayField>
    <errorMessage>Property Address and Email are both required before this lead can be converted.</errorMessage>
</ValidationRule>
